High-level view of what the simplifier files in this directory do

Ordinary develop clients need no migration. Extensions depend on ordinary
and shared facilities, never the reverse. Ordinary simpLib/congLib imports
omit extension strategies, source inventories, split caches/registrations
and the opt-in tracked default provider. Signatures define the compiled API;
notes.md and ../tests/compatibility/migration/TASK27.md give the final
construction/type migration, module ownership and rebuilding caveats.

Cache.sml:     Caching for context-aware decision procedures.

Cond_rewr.sml: The fundamental rewriting-at-a-point implementation:
               the equivalent of REWRITE_TAC's REWR_CONV.  Handles
               side conditions, hence Cond(itional)_rewr(iting), and
               permutative equations.

               Also includes the fundamental functions for
               transforming arbitrary theorems into rewrite rules
               (e.g.,  p /\ q  --> [p, q])

Cond_rewrExt.sml: Explicit paired/configured conditional compilation.
               Tracked preparation binds both runners to the actual
               bounded control; projections do not recompile or reset it.

SimpTracking.sml: Internal shared thread-local rewrite reporter used by
               both conditional engines. No extension registrations.

Opening.sml:   Moving into a term under the control of a congruence
               rule.

OpeningExt.sml, TravrulesExt.sml:
               Explicit threaded congruence construction. Alias the original
               congproc/preorder/travrules types rather than copying them.

Satisfy.sml:   Simplistic code to try to simplify existential goals
               through unification and examination of context.
               Available through the simpset fragment in
               SatisfySimps.

Sequence.sml:  A lazy list implementation, used only in Satisfy.sml.

Trace.sml:     Support for outputting trace messages, with increased
               verbosity elicited when reference variable is set
               higher.

Traverse.sml:  High-level specification of traversal strategy.
               Roughly, this is
                 do rewrites at current level as much as possible,
                 then descend.  When you come back from this, if
                 something changed, then try for another rewrite.  If
                 there is one, loop.  Otherwise, try a decision
                 procedures.  If any succeeds, loop.

TraverseExt.sml:
               Distinct extended reducer/configuration/policy types;
               explicit ordinary reducer lifting, refreshing contexts,
               root/context/observed and child-first traversal. No reverse
               adapter, implicit promotion or opaque source discovery.

Travrules.sml: Generic datatype for storing information on how to
               traverse terms.  This types stores congruence rule
               procedures, which come from the Opening module

Unify.sml:     Implementation of first-order unification.  Used only
               in Satisfy.sml.

Unwind.sml:    One-point eliminations of variables under universal and
               existential quantifiers.  Turns
                  (?x. P x /\ (x = 4) /\ Q x)
               into
                  P 4 /\ Q 4

boolSimps.sml: Basic simplification data for booleans.  Includes
               congruence rules for implications, conditional
               expressions and conjunctions.

combinSimps.sml:
               Simplification data for combinators.  Just a collection
               of rewrites.

pureSimpsExt.sml, boolSimpsExt.sml, combinSimpsExt.sml:
               Independent tracked recipes built from ingredients, not
               imports of installed ordinary simpsets. Threaded congruence
               and ETA are explicit choices. Later typed numeric/set/list/
               integer/real catalogs and src/boss/trackedSimpDefaults build
               an explicit ordered recipe/provider; no automatic ordinary
               update mirroring. The provider is not in ordinary hol.state.

pureSimps.sml: A simpset that transforms rewrites according to
               mk_cond_rewr from Cond_rewr.sml, but wrapping each in
               the BOUNDED/UNBOUNDED tag.

SplitData.sml: Private split-rule event stream, attribute ownership and
               context-selecting dispatcher; explicit initialization only.

simpMarkerScript.sml, simpMarkerLib.sml:
               Simplifier-owned Split/ExcludeX constants and recursive
               tactic argument processing. Legacy markerLib is unchanged.

splitLib.sml:  Pure/local datatype splitting and explicit persistent-rule
               registration. Queries alone claim no attribute namespace.

splitPersistLib.sml:
               Explicit opt-in module for split-bearing theory scripts.
               Record it with Theory.add_ML_dependency in exports so fresh
               imports initialize before theory-data replay.

selftest.sml:  Complete unchanged develop regression input. Extension tests
               execute in separate processes under ../tests; no extension
               prerequisite is linked into this ordinary launcher. The full
               native suite is ../tests/native-extension/selftest.sml.
               ../tests/api-audit checks actual fresh paths, callbacks,
               control identities and executable migration examples.

simpLib.sml:   Puts it all together. The simpset data structure is
               implemented here, as is the code that wraps up
               user-supplied conversions and rewrites, and makes them
               fit into the simplifier's data structures.

simpExtLib.sml:
               Separate opaque tracked simpsets/fragments, paired runners,
               source handles/views/bundles, preserving replay, strategies,
               extended markers and explicit configured/global tactics.
               Source slots/serials belong here alone. Projections share
               actual installed controls and do not compile or collect.
               No arbitrary ordinary set import or ssfrags_of reconstruction.

congLib.sml:   Ordinary preorder simplification with ordinary simpsets.

congExtLib.sml:
               Explicit configured preorder simplification on extension
               simpsets/congsets; lifts public ordinary fragments only.

Shared identities:
               Cond_rewr owns the sole stack_limit; Trace owns the original
               action, hook, level and registered trace knob. SimpTracking
               owns one reporter slot; BoundedRewrites owns actual quota
               refs. Both engines use original Context/types/exceptions.
               Named fragment registries are deliberately different typed
               slots, simpLib.ssfragDB and simpExtLib.ssfragDB, with no
               cross-engine lookup fallback. SplitData/splitLib are single
               simplifier-owned modules; generic markerLib, ThmSetData and
               postkernel machinery are not extended for this split.
